# UI Design Standards (Tailwind v4 + shadcn-svelte)

Apply a **top UI designer** lens: clarity, consistency, accessibility, and zero fighting the design system.

## Stack (do not mix alternatives)

- **Tailwind CSS v4** — utilities + `@theme` in `src/routes/layout.css` only. No `tailwind.config.js`.
- **shadcn-svelte** — style `nova`, base `zinc`, icons `@lucide/svelte`.
- **Theme** — `mode-watcher` + `.dark` class. Tokens: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, etc.
- **Add primitives**: `pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add <name> -y` — never hand-copy from docs.

## Use shadcn components only (required)

All interactive and structural UI must come from **`$lib/components/ui/**`** (installed via shadcn-svelte). Do not invent parallel primitives.

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Loading placeholders | `Skeleton` from `$lib/components/ui/skeleton` |
| Buttons / links-as-buttons | `Button` |
| Cards | `Card` |
| Inputs / textarea / label | `Input`, `Textarea`, `Label` |
| Dialogs / sheets / menus | `Dialog`, `Sheet`, `DropdownMenu`, etc. |
| Badges / separators / tooltips | `Badge`, `Separator`, `Tooltip` |
| Sidebar chrome | `Sidebar` |

```svelte
<!-- ✅ shadcn Skeleton -->
import { Skeleton } from '$lib/components/ui/skeleton/index.js';
<Skeleton class="h-4 w-2/5" />

<!-- ❌ Hand-rolled pulse placeholder when Skeleton exists -->
<div class="bg-muted h-4 w-2/5 animate-pulse rounded-md"></div>
```

- If a primitive is missing: **add it** with `pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add <name> -y`, then use it.
- App-level wrappers in `$lib/components/**` may compose shadcn parts; they must not reimplement Button/Skeleton/Input/etc.
- Never copy third-party component source into the repo when shadcn already provides it.

## File boundaries (prevents conflicts)

```
src/routes/layout.css           # ONLY global theme + @layer base — no page-specific rules
src/lib/components/ui/**      # shadcn primitives — edit only when customizing the design system
src/lib/components/**         # app shells (sidebar, header) — compose ui/* here
src/routes/**/*.svelte        # pages — layout + content; no deep style overrides on ui/*
```

- **Never** edit `ui/*` for one-off page needs — wrap or compose in app components.
- **Never** add second CSS frameworks or global resets that compete with shadcn `base` layer.

## Composition rules

```svelte
<!-- ✅ Compose shadcn primitives -->
import * as Card from '$lib/components/ui/card/index.js';
import { Button } from '$lib/components/ui/button/index.js';
import { cn } from '$lib/utils.js';

<div class={cn('flex flex-col gap-4', className)}>...</div>

<!-- ❌ Raw HTML styled from scratch when shadcn has the part -->
<button class="rounded bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2">...</button>

<!-- ❌ Conflicting utilities on ui components -->
<Button class="!bg-red-500 !p-8 z-[9999]">...</Button>
```

- Prefer **variants** (`variant`, `size`) over `!important` or arbitrary overrides.
- Merge classes with **`cn()`** from `$lib/utils.js` — never string-concatenate Tailwind classes.
- Use **`$lib/components/ui/.../index.js`** import paths (matches generated components).

## Tailwind v4 practices

- **Semantic colors only** in components: `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-sidebar-accent` — not `bg-zinc-900` unless chart/data viz.
- **Spacing rhythm**: `gap-2`, `gap-4`, `gap-6`, `p-4`, `p-6` — stay on the scale; avoid random `p-[13px]`.
- **Responsive**: mobile-first — `flex-col md:flex-row`, `grid md:grid-cols-2`. Sidebar already collapses; don’t hard-code desktop-only layouts.
- **Typography**: `text-sm` for UI chrome, `text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight` for page titles — don’t invent new scales per page.
- **Radius**: use `--radius` tokens (`rounded-lg`, `rounded-md`) — aligned with nova preset.

## shadcn-svelte patterns (Svelte 5)

- **Runes**: `$props()`, `$state`, `$derived` — no `export let`.
- **Links in sidebar/nav**: `Sidebar.MenuButton` + `{#snippet child({ props })}` + `<a href="..." {...props}>`.
- **Icons**: `@lucide/svelte/icons/<name>` — `class="size-4"` (shadcn default icon size).
- **Active nav**: `isActive={page.url.pathname === href}` from `$app/state`.
- **Dialogs / sheets**: one overlay at a time — use shadcn `Dialog` or `Sheet`; don’t stack custom `fixed inset-0 z-50` divs.

### Sheet & Dialog (bits-ui)

Use the shadcn primitives end-to-end — don’t hand-roll portaled side panels.

```svelte
<!-- ✅ Trigger inside Sheet.Root — child snippet forwards bits-ui props -->
<Sheet.Root bind:open>
	<Sheet.Trigger>
		{#snippet child({ props })}
			<Button variant="ghost" type="button" {...props}>Open</Button>
		{/snippet}
	</Sheet.Trigger>
	<Sheet.Content side="right" class="sm:max-w-md">
		<!-- content -->
	</Sheet.Content>
</Sheet.Root>

<!-- ❌ Trigger outside Root + manual open — breaks context/ARIA; avoid -->
<Button onclick={() => (open = true)}>...</Button>
<Sheet.Root bind:open>...</Sheet.Root>
```

- **Overlay:** Use the default sheet overlay unless there is a strong reason not to. Match existing panels (e.g. profile menu ↔ module Details in `workspace-module-card.svelte`). Default: `bg-black/10` + `backdrop-blur-xs` from `sheet-overlay.svelte` — not heavy `bg-black/40 backdrop-blur-md`.
- **Portal wrappers:** If editing `sheet.svelte`, `dialog.svelte`, `sheet-portal.svelte`, or `dialog-portal.svelte`, explicitly pass `{children}` / `{child}` snippets to bits-ui — don’t rely on `{...restProps}` alone for snippet props.
- **ObjectId route params:** Use `[id=objectId]` with `src/params/objectId.ts` — see **`sveltekit-mongodb-engineering.mdc`** (no `mongodb` in matchers).

## Avoid blocking & z-index wars

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| Let Dialog/Sheet/Dropdown set overlay z-index | Add `z-[9999]` on random wrappers |
| Use `Sidebar.Provider` + `Sidebar.Inset` for app shell | Nest multiple `fixed` headers that overlap |
| `min-h-0` + `flex-1` for scroll regions inside layout | `h-screen` on every nested child |
| `truncate` / `min-w-0` in flex rows for long text | Fixed widths that break mobile |
| Portal-based menus (bits-ui defaults) | `overflow-hidden` on ancestors that clip popovers |

## Dark mode

- Toggle via **`toggleMode`** / **`ModeWatcher`** — don’t per-component `dark:` color one-offs that ignore tokens.
- Test both modes when changing `layout.css` variables.
- Sidebar/docs: use token pairs (`sidebar`, `sidebar-foreground`) — don’t hardcode light-only colors.

## Accessibility (non-negotiable)

- Interactive controls: shadcn `Button`, `Input`, etc. — they carry focus rings (`focus-visible:ring-*`).
- Icon-only buttons: **`aria-label`** (see `theme-toggle.svelte`).
- Don’t remove `outline-none` without providing visible focus — shadcn already handles this.
- Form labels: use shadcn `Label` + `Field` patterns when forms are added.

## Form placeholders

**Do not use `placeholder` on labeled form inputs** — labels (and optional helper text) carry the meaning.

| Use `placeholder` | Do not use `placeholder` |
|-------------------|--------------------------|
| Search / filter inputs (`Command.Input`, combobox search) | Text, email, password, tel, URL fields with a visible `Form.Label` |
| Unlabeled global search bars | Address, select-adjacent inputs, admin action fields |
| Rare cases with no room for a label — prefer `aria-label` instead | Example values (“Acme Services”, `https://…`, phone samples) |

**Select / combobox empty state** is not an HTML placeholder — keep trigger copy like “Select team size” or `FormCombobox`’s `placeholder` prop when nothing is selected.

```svelte
<!-- ✅ Labeled field — no placeholder -->
<Form.Label required>Workspace name</Form.Label>
<Input {...props} bind:value={$form.name} autocomplete="organization" />

<!-- ✅ Search inside combobox — placeholder allowed -->
<Command.Input placeholder={searchPlaceholder} />

<!-- ❌ Redundant example placeholder on a labeled field -->
<Input placeholder="Acme Services" bind:value={$form.name} />
```

- Optional fields: mark with `(optional)` on the label, not a placeholder.
- Inline compact inputs without a visible label: use `aria-label` (see admin reject reason).

## When adding new UI

1. Check if shadcn has the component → `pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add <name> -y`.
2. Build app-level wrapper in `src/lib/components/` if reused across routes.
3. Page stays thin — cards, tables, forms composed from primitives.
4. If theme must change globally → update `layout.css` tokens, not individual pages.
5. Run `pnpm check` after Svelte changes.

## List / table search

Place search **top-right** in the card header via **`Card.Action`** — never left-aligned above the table body.

- Component: **`ListSearchInput`** (`$lib/components/list/list-search-input.svelte`)
- Width: `sm:w-52 lg:w-60`, height `h-10`, muted background (`bg-muted/40`)
- Parent owns `searchQuery` state; pass it into the list/table component as a prop
- Use `aria-label` (no visible label); placeholder is allowed for search fields

```svelte
<Card.Header>
	<Card.Title>Workspace members</Card.Title>
	<Card.Description>…</Card.Description>
	<Card.Action>
		<ListSearchInput bind:value={searchQuery} placeholder="Search members..." ariaLabel="Search members" />
	</Card.Action>
</Card.Header>
```

## Auth forms (`src/routes/(auth)/**`)

Use shared tokens from **`$lib/auth/ui.ts`** — do not invent per-page button heights or link styles.

| Element | Standard |
|--------|----------|
| Full-width actions (submit, OAuth, navigation `Button`) | `class={AUTH_ACTION_BUTTON_CLASS}` → `h-10 w-full` |
| Inline footer link (“Sign in”, “Sign up”) | `class={AUTH_INLINE_LINK_CLASS}` inside `text-muted-foreground text-center text-sm` |
| Submit / OAuth busy state | `cn(AUTH_ACTION_BUTTON_CLASS, authLoading.authBusy && 'pointer-events-none cursor-wait')` |
| Page title | `text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight` via `AuthFormPanel` |
| Body / helper copy | `text-sm` + `text-muted-foreground` |
| Form field spacing | `space-y-5` within forms; `space-y-6` between sections |

```svelte
import { AUTH_ACTION_BUTTON_CLASS, AUTH_INLINE_LINK_CLASS } from '$lib/auth/ui';

<Button type="submit" class={cn(AUTH_ACTION_BUTTON_CLASS, busy && 'pointer-events-none cursor-wait')}>
	Sign in
</Button>

<p class="text-muted-foreground text-center text-sm">
	Already have an account?
	<a href="/login" class={AUTH_INLINE_LINK_CLASS}>Sign in</a>
</p>
```

- **Never** use `<Button class="w-full">` without `AUTH_ACTION_BUTTON_CLASS` on auth screens — default shadcn height is `h-8`.
- **Never** mix raw `text-primary font-medium hover:underline` on auth footer links; use `AUTH_INLINE_LINK_CLASS`.
- Google OAuth button: `GoogleSignInButton` (already uses `AUTH_ACTION_BUTTON_CLASS`).

## Status alerts (info, warning, danger, success, plain)

**Every inline status message must include an icon.** Use **`StatusAlert`** from `$lib/components/status-alert.svelte` — never hand-roll colored `div`s for feedback.

**Every alert must have both a title and subtext (`description`).** Never show a single-line alert body without a headline. Map shared copy in `$lib/shared/auth-messages.ts` via `resolveAuthFormAlertPresentation()`.

| Variant | Use for | Icon (`@lucide/svelte`) |
|--------|---------|-------------------------|
| `info` | Neutral guidance, **“Check your email”**, tips | `info` (blue / `text-primary`) |
| `warning` | Rate limits, caution, recoverable issues | `triangle-alert` |
| `danger` | Errors, invalid input, failed actions | `triangle-alert` (red / `text-destructive`) |
| `success` | Confirmed actions (password updated, email verified) | `circle-check` |
| `plain` | Low-emphasis notes without semantic color | `info` (muted) |

**Icon rules (non-negotiable):**
- **“Check your email”** and similar inbox-guidance alerts → always `variant="info"` (blue, `info` icon) — never `success`/green.
- **Errors and danger** → always `triangle-alert` — never `circle-alert`.

```svelte
import StatusAlert from '$lib/components/status-alert.svelte';

<StatusAlert
	variant="success"
	title="Password updated"
	description="Sign in with your new password."
/>
<StatusAlert
	variant="warning"
	title="Too many attempts"
	description="Try again in 2:00."
/>
<StatusAlert
	variant="danger"
	title="Verification failed"
	description="That verification code is invalid or has expired."
/>
<StatusAlert
	variant="info"
	title="Check your email"
	description="We sent a verification code to your email."
/>
```

- **`FormAlert`** (`$lib/components/auth/form-alert.svelte`) — shorthand for `variant="danger"`; requires `title` + `description`.
- **`AuthFormMessageAlert`** — wraps `StatusAlert`; resolves `title` + `description` from `resolveAuthFormAlertPresentation()`; auto-uses `warning` for rate-limit countdowns.
- **One alert at a time** — show a single alert per form or page section. When a new status appears, **replace** the previous alert — never stack two banners. Use a mutually exclusive `{#if}` / `{:else if}` chain ordered by priority:
  1. Client errors (reCAPTCHA, validation)
  2. Form action errors (`$formMessage` from superforms)
  3. Redirect / query-param errors (`?error=…`, Google OAuth)
  4. Success or info banners (`?reset=success`, “check your email”) — lowest priority; hide when any error is active

```svelte
{#if recaptchaError}
	<AuthFormMessageAlert message={recaptchaError} />
{:else if $formMessage}
	<AuthFormMessageAlert message={$formMessage} bind:limited={formRateLimited} />
{:else if data.googleAuthError}
	<AuthFormMessageAlert message={data.googleAuthError} retryAfterSeconds={data.rateLimitRetryAfter} />
{:else if data.passwordResetSuccess}
	<StatusAlert variant="success" title="Password updated" description="Sign in with your new password." />
{/if}
```
- **Alert copy** — prefer structured `title` + `description` mappings in `$lib/shared/auth-messages.ts`. Title = short headline; description = supporting detail or next step. Unmapped messages fall back to `AUTH_ALERT_FALLBACK_TITLE` + message as description.
- Icons: `class="size-4 shrink-0"` in the component; `aria-hidden="true"` on decorative icons. `role="alert"` for danger/warning; `role="status"` for info/success/plain.

## Red flags (reject in review)

- New global CSS outside `layout.css`
- Modified `src/lib/components/ui/**` for a single page
- Raw hex/rgb in `.svelte` files instead of CSS variables
- Duplicate button/input styles
- Auth `Button` with only `w-full` (missing `h-10` via `AUTH_ACTION_BUTTON_CLASS`)
- Inline status `div` with only background/border colors and no icon — use `StatusAlert`
- Stacked status alerts on the same form (success + error visible together) — use one mutually exclusive alert slot
- `StatusAlert` with only a title or only body text — always pass both `title` and `description`
- Hand-rolled Skeleton / Button / Input / Dialog when `$lib/components/ui/*` already has it — add via `pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add` instead
- Auth alerts with unmapped copy and no entry in `$lib/shared/auth-messages.ts` when the message is reused
- “Check your email” alerts using `variant="success"` or green styling — use `variant="info"`
- Danger/error alerts using `circle-alert` — use `triangle-alert`
- `placeholder` on labeled `Input` / `Textarea` fields (use labels + helper text instead)
- Multiple competing layout roots (second sidebar, second header provider)
- `!` important utilities on shadcn components
